=== ARTICLE: Silhouette - under the hood ===
[size=4][b]What this covers[/b][/size]
How Silhouette picks, builds and applies bodies, with the numbers behind the Silhouette page. It follows OBody NG's design, config keys, priority and API names, and works through LooksMenu's own BodyGen, so the bodies are LooksMenu's and stay in your save.

[size=4][b]The picker window[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Aim at anyone, or at no one for yourself, and press the hotkey (or the MCM button).[/*]
[*]The window shows every preset that fits their body as a grid of pictures: 384 with a picture, 196 women and 188 men.[/*]
[*]Six filters: All, People, Plain, Rough, Fine and Yours.[/*]
[*]A click puts the body on them live while the camera frames them and they stand still. Apply keeps it; Cancel puts back exactly what they had.[/*]
[*]The hotkey lists (Pick, Next, Previous, Keep, Cancel) have no length limit, past Papyrus's 128-entry cap.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]It measures your install instead of assuming it[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]A preset whose sliders your body's [font=Courier New].tri[/font] does not have would do nothing, so it is left out.[/*]
[*]If your base body was not built zeroed, Silhouette names the exact preset it was built from and the zeroed one to rebuild with, instead of stacking every NPC on top of it.[/*]
[*]Every body it writes is rebuilt the way LooksMenu builds it and checked to land on its preset.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Silhouette's own bodies[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]41 bodies per sex, 82 in all, generated and measured rather than hand-picked, so no two look alike.[/*]
[*]18 Plain, 17 Rough (very fat, very flat, frail, disproportioned) and 6 Fine, drawn at 70 / 22 / 8 %.[/*]
[*]The NPC picker also offers the stock CBBE and BodyTalk presets and your own BodySlide presets, read from BodySlide's SliderPresets folder when the game starts, exactly as BodySlide builds them. None of them is ever random.[/*]
[*]A test holds the plugin to the generator's own reading of your presets: 6 of 6 presets and 142 values identical.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Named people and factions[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]60 companions and named NPCs, 30 women and 30 men, each with a body that fits who they are.[/*]
[*]The Diamond City pack is sardonic on purpose. Each body is the mod's own body built with that character's values, drawn at one scale over the standard body.[/*]
[*]Eleven factions draw from ten bodies per sex in their own look. That is 220 bodies, measured like the pool.[/*]
[*]The faction picture shows each faction's bodies by overall size and belly. Size is the sum of seven girths.[/*]
[*]Faction rules read an NPC record's own factions, as OBody does, not its templates'.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]One body mod is enough[/b][/size]
Women are made for CBBE and men for BodyTalk. With only one of them installed, Silhouette leaves the other sex alone: no rolls, rules, resets or picks for them. Silhouette.log says why, and a message box tells you once a launch. Reset everyone logs each person and the body they got.

[size=4][b]Old saves[/b][/size]
A save that never had Silhouette gets bodies for everyone on its first load, once, with a notification (39 people on one old save). A switch in MCM turns it off.

[size=4][b]Clothing: ORefit[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]While someone is dressed, their breasts are held together and lifted, and under heavy clothes their nipples are flattened.[/*]
[*]Heavy is told by the item's name (armor, jacket, coat, parka and more, whole words only), not by its slot. You can name items heavy or light yourself.[/*]
[*]ORefit only ever raises a slider, under a keyword of its own, so the moment they undress they are exactly their own body. It cannot lower a slider, because LooksMenu keeps the highest value per keyword.[/*]
[*]Heavy clothes are told by English names; a localized game needs its words added to [font=Courier New]heavyWords[/font].[/*]
[*]The flattening shows only on outfits whose meshes carry the refit sliders: mod outfits built with them. No vanilla or DLC heavy outfit does.[/*]
[*]Measured over the author's 816-plugin load order: 137 garments flattened under the old slot rule, 35 under the name rule, and no bra, top or shirt among them any more.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Variety[/b][/size]
Every person has their own nipples (size, areola, tip, length) and, on the anatomy bodies, their own genital shape. Every man gets his own ball size on BodyTalk. These are never a runtime state: scenes own them. The dots in the variety picture are real people from the author's save, each inside the range the mesh was measured for.

[size=4][b]Other mods[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]AAF-aware: anyone in a scene waits, and their change lands when the scene ends.[/*]
[*]Other mods' morphs under their own keyword are never touched. People another mod marked before Silhouette arrived get a body within a 24-hour window, keeping that mod's morphs.[/*]
[*]Anatomy's arousal keeps nipples flat under armour Silhouette marks heavy.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]One DLL, two game versions[/b][/size]
One DLL runs on old-gen and Anniversary through Runtime Database. Before touching anyone it checks the 11 class members it reads on the running game, and switches itself off rather than run half on. It is proven in game on both; on Anniversary 1.11.240 it read 39 bodies with 0 failures. There is no custom menu, to stay clear of a known plugin-menu crash on 1.10.163: the picker is MCM and hotkeys.
